[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we need to maximize the real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(z\) is a complex number with \(|z| = 4\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in polar form as \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\). Then we can substitute \(z\) into the expression and separate the real and imaginary parts.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m The expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m (75 + 117i) \cdot 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m First, let's simplify the terms:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m (75 + 117i) \cdot 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + 4i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} \cdot \frac{\cos\theta - i\sin\theta}{\cos\theta - i\sin\theta} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)}{4(\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta)} = \frac{96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta + i(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)}{4} = 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta + i(36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m Combining these, the expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + 4i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta) + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta + i(36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m = (4 \cdot 75\cos\theta - 4 \cdot 117\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta) + i(4 \cdot 75\sin\theta + 4 \cdot 117\cos\theta + 36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m = (300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta) + i(300\sin\theta + 468\cos\theta + 36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m = (324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta) + i(336\cos\theta + 276\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m The real part of the expression is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m 324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m To maximize \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\), we can use the method of finding the maximum value of a linear combination of sine and cosine. The maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = -432\), so the maximum value is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + 432^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 186624} = \sqrt{291600} = 540
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=475120)[0m Thus, the largest possible real part of the expression is \(\boxed{540}\).
